The loop is rewritten to use a raw pointer and an unsigned index, so the vector's size and data pointer are read once instead of on every iteration. Behavior is unchanged: it returns `FIT_TRUE` on the first field whose `GetNum()` matches, and `FIT_FALSE` otherwise. The speedup is likely small, since the function is a linear scan.

```cpp
FIT_BOOL Mesg::HasField(const int fieldNum) const
{
    const Field* data = fields.data();
    const size_t n = fields.size();
    for (size_t i = 0; i < n; ++i)
    {
        if (data[i].GetNum() == fieldNum)
            return FIT_TRUE;
    }

    return FIT_FALSE;
}
```